1
00:00:00,247 --> 00:00:07,287
You launched a paid API for AI agents. It looks fine. But agents can't pay it, and nothing tells you why.

2
00:00:08,519 --> 00:00:14,236
x402 Doctor checks your endpoint the way a paying agent would, without spending a cent.

3
00:00:14,695 --> 00:00:21,906
In seconds you see every check: the 402 challenge, each payment option, the Solana payout account, discovery.

4
00:00:22,362 --> 00:00:32,111
And for every problem, exactly what to change. Here, the price is written as dollars instead of token units, and the Solana option is missing its fee payer.

5
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:34,228
Fix it, and run it again.

6
00:00:35,633 --> 00:00:37,489
Every check passes: green.

7
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,681
That's for sellers. For buyers, there's something new.

8
00:00:41,149 --> 00:00:50,834
Before your agent pays an unknown API, it asks the Doctor first, for a tenth of a cent, paid on Base, Solana, the XRP Ledger or Algorand.

9
00:00:51,288 --> 00:00:59,971
Go, caution, or no-go. Plus the cheapest payment option that will actually settle, and whether the price is in line with comparable services.

10
00:01:03,087 --> 00:01:12,239
And every day, we check every x402 endpoint in the Coinbase Bazaar. Almost forty thousand, from about nineteen thousand distinct services.

11
00:01:12,713 --> 00:01:18,964
Each one gets a thirty-day track record, so agents know who's reliable, and sellers can see their own score.

12
00:01:19,444 --> 00:01:23,540
x402 Doctor. Free on the web, pay-per-call for agents.

